      "writtenOn": "2017-10-18T17:01:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function is called for HOOK_INIT which would be called in RO case as well. Maybe need a better name for the function? lpc_init_mask() instead of the lpc_post_sysjump_restore_mask()\n\nThe way it works is:\non cold boot: EC will set LPC_HOST_EVENT_ALWAYS_REPORT mask by default. Other masks will be just initialized to 0 until explicitly set by the host.\n\non sysjump: EC will set LPC_HOST_EVENT_ALWAYS_REPORT and just override it with the values in sysjump saved data.\n\nFor the case you mentioned:\n1. RW update which modifies the default mask: I think we would have to do more than just this. As you indicated we will need a callback into board to allow this.\n\n2. Feature being deployed in RW but not RO: That would not work too since memcpy below will update it to whatever RO has saved.\n\nI feel like we should at least support #2 above. Let me rework this a bit more, something like this:\n\n1. Add a new function lpc_init_mask which is called upon HOOK_INIT\n2. lpc_init_mask will first call into lpc_post_sysjump_restore_mask and then set LPC_HOST_EVENT_ALWAYS_REPORT to default mask. I can add a weak function here to return LPC_HOST_EVENT_ALWAYS_REPORT_DEFAULT_MASK by default and it can be overriden by boards at any time.",
      "parentUuid": "4de5476b_92f0e901",
      "revId": "91603a37c2fc21033f797796d3921164dc5c9c93",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
